    "alert_id": "EX2_002",
    "title": "Plan lacks creatinine recheck after rehydration",
    "message": "Guidelines emphasise checking creatinine in hospitalised TDF patients because intercurrent illness with dehydration may cause renal deterioration. The clinician's plan includes IV fluid resuscitation and empiric antibiotics but does not mention repeat creatinine monitoring after rehydration. Without a follow-up creatinine, the clinician cannot determine whether the AKI is resolving with treatment or persisting, which is essential before making a permanent decision about TDF. A repeat creatinine within 24–48 hours of fluid resuscitation would clarify whether TDF discontinuation is warranted.",
